    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0779" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>

                <head>291. Note From the Presidentʼs Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to President Nixon<anchor n="1" xml:id="d291-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-09-09">September 9, 1970</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>In view of the Middle East situation<anchor n="2" xml:id="d291-f2"/> this is an
                    ideal time to proceed rapidly with the announcement of resumption of U.S.
                    military assistance to Greece. It will also assist in creating a favorable
                    climate in the event we have to call on Greek cooperation should a contingency
                    occur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Henry A. Kissinger</hi>
                        <anchor n="3" xml:id="d291-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d291-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d291-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 593,
                    Country Files, Middle East, Greece, Vol. I, Jan 69–Oct 70. No classification
                    marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d291-f2" n="2" xml:id="d291-f2-content">
                <p>On August 26 fighting broke out between Palestinian and Jordanian forces.
                    Beginning on September 6, a series of Western airliners were seized by
                    terrorists and flown to Jordan where the crews and passengers were held hostage.
                    See <ref target="frus1969-76ve01#d45">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1969–1976, volume E–1,
                        Documents on Global Issues, 1969–1972, Document 45</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d291-f3" n="3" xml:id="d291-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
